<title>GERMANY: Lamfalussy says EMU delay speculation unfounded.</title>
<headline>Lamfalussy says EMU delay speculation unfounded.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Monetary Institute (EMI) president Alexandre Lamfalussy said on Monday that recent speculation about a delay in European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) was unfounded.</p>
<p>Speaking to reporters on the fringe of a banking conference in Frankfurt, Lamfalussy said: &quot;All these market rumours about a delay are unfounded.&quot;</p>
</text>
